2026-02-15 14:22:46,060 [DEBUG] anthropic._base_client: Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-68920d6a-948f-496e-ba21-45a75cf7373b', 'content': None, 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 256, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Analyze this job listing and extract the following fields. Return ONLY valid JSON, no other text.\n\nJob Title: Associate General Counsel, Policy (LATAM)\nOrganization: OpenAI\nLocation: São Paulo\nDescription:\nAbout the Team OpenAI\'s Legal team plays a crucial role in furthering OpenAI\'s mission by tackling innovative, fundamental legal issues in AI. If you\'re passionate about doing significant and unique work as a technology lawyer, this team is for you. The team comprises professionals from diverse fields, including technology, AI, privacy, IP, competition, corporate, employment, tax law, regulatory, and litigation. About the Role We’re seeking an Associate General Counsel to help navigate the increasing AI legislative and regulatory landscape in Brazil and broader Latin America. We’re looking for a legal self-starter, who is comfortable jumping into a deep dive of laws applicable to AI, as well as a broad range of AI regulatory issues that will help shape AI policy going forward and for which there is little precedent. This role reports to our Deputy General Counsel for International & Policy Legal. This role is based in São Paulo. In this role, you will: - Analyze laws and regulations in Brazil and broader LATAM concerning AI to understand their impact on OpenAI and the broader AI community. - Develop policy positions on pending legislation and international standards. - Provide legal analysis and advice to the Global Affairs team and other internal stakeholders. - Contribute to our ongoing improvements to AI governance as regulations come into force. - Monitor and keep the team updated on emerging legislative and regulatory developments related to AI in the LATAM region. You might thrive in this role if you have: - 15+ years of legal experience. - Strong leadership and ability to influence. - Combination of an in-house company, government/institution, or law firm experience. - Strong background in Brazil and LATAM technology laws. - Experience and familiarity with AI. - Knowledge and experience with intellectual property laws. - Create clear and concise writing, distilling complex concepts into simple, explainable, and persuasive ideas - Experience analyzing complex legislation. - Cross-border experience, particularly in the countries in the LATAM region. - Experience engaging with regulators and/or policymakers. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these keys:\n- "work_mode": one of "Remote (Global)", "Remote (US)", "Remote (EU)", "Hybrid", "In-Person", or null if unclear\n- "visa_sponsorship": true, false, or null if not mentioned\n- "seniority_level": one of "Entry", "Mid", "Senior", "All Levels", or null if unclear\n\nRules:\n- "Entry" = internship, fellowship, junior, entry-level, 0-2 years experience\n- "Mid" = mid-level, 3-7 years experience\n- "Senior" = senior, lead, director, head, principal, 8+ years experience\n- "All Levels" = explicitly states open to multiple levels\n- For work_mode, if it says "remote" without geographic restriction, use "Remote (Global)"\n- For visa_sponsorship, only set true/false if explicitly mentioned'}], 'model': 'claude-haiku-4-5'}}
